Hi @JBoschma, the clipping is the default expected behavior for ImPlot3D as of now (I'll probably change it later). You can use the flag `ImPlot3DFlags_NoClip` to avoid clipping.

```cpp
if (ImPlot3D::BeginPlot("Surface Plots", ImVec2(-1, 400), ImPlot3DFlags_NoClip)) {
    ...
    ImPlot3D::EndPlot();
}
```

Please let me know if this resolves your issue.

> A title that is outside a clipping rectangle where the actual plotting takes place. In the lower demo that clipping area could be the yellow rectangle. The plot then never interferes with the title.

Great, I agree with you.

> And the plot-axes could be made a little bit smaller. When rotating the default size plot, the axes labels and ticks are then always within the clipping area, are not clipped, and do not interfere with the title.

