Hi @JBoschma! The PR with the fix for this was just merged into `main`.

- The plot data/labels don't overlap with the title anymore (title will always be visible).
- There is a new style variable `ImPlot3DStyleVar_ViewScaleFactor` to control the plot scaling; you can adjust it to ensure the labels are not clipped for you. If this variable is set to `0.5f`, for example, the plot would get twice smaller.

### Demo video
https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8972b451-c617-4013-91a1-db1cfb96e919

### Usage example
```cpp
// Global setting for all plots
ImPlot3D::GetStyle().ViewScaleFactor = 0.8f; // More conservative spacing

// Per-plot setting
ImPlot3D::PushStyleVar(ImPlot3DStyleVar_ViewScaleFactor, 1.2f);
if (ImPlot3D::BeginPlot("My Plot")) {
    // Plot with larger area, less margin
    ImPlot3D::EndPlot();
}
ImPlot3D::PopStyleVar();
```

