You calculate an AABB over all vertices, but you pass an indexed mesh to tinybvh. Could it be that you don't use all vertices?

---

This indeed seems the case. Verify with this aabb calculation in TestMain.cpp:

````  float xmin = 1000, ymin = 1000, zmin = 1000, xmax = -1000, ymax = -1000, zmax = -1000;
  for( int i = 0; i < meshData.indices.size(); i++ )
  {
	auto p = meshData.vertices[meshData.indices[i]];
	if (p.x < xmin) xmin = p.x;
	if (p.y < ymin) ymin = p.y;
	if (p.z < zmin) zmin = p.z;
	if (p.x > xmax) xmax = p.x;
	if (p.y > ymax) ymax = p.y;
	if (p.z > zmax) zmax = p.z;
  }
````

---

By the way, you should be able to use glm directly in TinyBVH. I didn't try this though; would love to have your feedback on this feature. Have a look at tiny_bvh.h lines 37-51; it involves defining ````TINYBVH_USE_CUSTOM_VECTOR_TYPES````, after which you can specify which glm types should replace tinybvh types.

