Hello developers of SKRTOS_sparrow,
I have identified a potential **NULL pointer dereference (NPD)** vulnerability in the code at `rbtree/Sparrow/timer/timer.c#L57`.

The function `rb_first` may return NULL when the red-black tree ClockTree is empty (i.e., ClockTree->rb_node == NULL). However, the returned node pointer is ​not checked for NULL​ before being dereferenced in the while loop condition (node->value).

The timer_check function is executed immediately after task creation via xTaskCreate. If the ClockTree is initialized as empty (via `rb_root_init`), the following sequence occurs:

- `rb_root_init` sets `ClockTree->rb_node = NULL`.
- `xTaskCreate` starts `timer_check`, which calls `rb_first(&ClockTree)`.
- `rb_first` returns NULL because the tree is empty.

The code proceeds to dereference node->value in while (node->value <= AbsoluteClock), causing a ​crash.

> Initialization (Empty Tree)

```c
void rb_root_init(rb_root_handle root)  
{  
    *root = (rb_root){  
        .rb_node = NULL,  // <--- Tree initialized as empty  
        .save_node = NULL,  
        .count = 0  
    };  
}  
```

> Task Creation

```c
TaskHandle_t xTimerInit(uint8_t timer_priority, uint16_t stack)  
{  
    TaskHandle_t self = NULL;  
    rb_root_init(&ClockTree);  
    xTaskCreate((TaskFunction_t)timer_check,  
                stack,  
                NULL,  
                timer_priority,  
                &self);  
    return self;  
}  
```

> Vulnerable Code

```c
void timer_check(void)  
{  
    while (1) {  
        rb_node *node = rb_first(&ClockTree);  
        while (node->value <= AbsoluteClock) {  // <--- NPD if node == NULL  
            timer_struct *timer = container_of(node, timer_struct, TimerNode);  
            timer->CallBackFun(timer);  
            if (timer->TimerStopFlag == stop) {  
                rb_remove_node(&ClockTree, &timer->TimerNode);  
            }  
            if (node != ClockTree.save_node) {  
                node = rb_next(node);  
            }  
        }  
    }  
}  
```

