_No response_

### Checklist

- [x] I've searched for existing issues
- [x] I'm willing to help implement a fix

comments.body:
This is to be expected, as you're generating a static object here:

```js
const styles = {
	fontSize: `${@fontSize}px`,
	backgroundColor: 'red',
};
```

What you want here is for `styles` to be tracked upon changes to its properties, so you can do this:

```js
const styles = track(() => ({
		fontSize: `${@fontSize}px`,
		backgroundColor: 'red',
}));

<span style={@styles} class="fontSize">{@fontSize}</span>
```

It works when you put it into JSX as internally it's re-evaluating and creating a new object each time something inside changes. It can't do this outside, as it might be intentionally for you to create a static object. So you just need to make the object tracked to get back the reactivity you desire.

