You need to be "calling" / rendering it.  Otherwise, it's just a declaration.  It's a strange way of doing it but it works.

```jsx
export default component App(){
  <svg width={20}
      height={20}
      fill={"red"}
      viewBox="0 0 30 10"
      preserveAspectRatio="none">
      component children(){
        <polygon points="0,0 30,0 15,10" />
      }
      <children />
  </svg>
```

 If you name it something other than `children`, capitalize the name.

