I ran into the same issue. before the fix is released, you can work around it by adding an alias in your `vite.config.ts`:

```ts
import path from 'path';

export default defineConfig({
  resolve: {
    alias: {
      'basecoat-css/basecoat': path.resolve(
        __dirname,
        './node_modules/basecoat-css/dist/js/basecoat.js'
      ),
    },
  },
});
```

This is an internal logic for Basecoat: if a component has a JavaScript file, we run an init function (e.g. [`initSidebar`](https://github.com/hunvreus/basecoat/blob/main/src/js/sidebar.js#L19)).

Once that init function has run successfully, we dispatch a `basecoat:initialized` event on the element (see [JavaScript events for the Sidebar](https://basecoatui.com/components/sidebar/#usage-html-js-4) for example) and also set `data-{COMPONENT_NAME}-initialized` to `true` so that we know not to try and init them again.

We do that since we are watching DOM changes with `MutationObserver()` so that even if you modify the content (for example using HTMX or a traditional AJAX call), we still initialize any component that may have been added to the DOM.

[For example, for sidebar](https://github.com/hunvreus/basecoat/blob/main/src/js/sidebar.js#L101-L116):

```JS
  (...)
  document.querySelectorAll('.sidebar:not([data-sidebar-initialized])').forEach(initSidebar);

  const observer = new MutationObserver((mutations) => {
    mutations.forEach((mutation) => {
      mutation.addedNodes.forEach((node) => {
        if (node.nodeType === Node.ELEMENT_NODE) {
          if (node.matches('.sidebar:not([data-sidebar-initialized])')) {
            initSidebar(node);
          }
          node.querySelectorAll('.sidebar:not([data-sidebar-initialized])').forEach(initSidebar);
        }
      });
    });
  });

  observer.observe(document.body, { childList: true, subtree: true });
  (...)
```

